1
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:47,040
<i>Ready to meet in the Otherworld?</i>

2
00:01:47,040 --> 00:01:49,840
<i>Coordinates refreshed. Explore without fear.</i>

3
00:01:57,333 --> 00:02:00,059
<i>How will we recognize each other?</i>

4
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:03,753
<i>Let's use our identities
in Age of Scorched Earth.</i>

5
00:02:10,459 --> 00:02:12,369
<i>Don't drink anything from strangers.</i>

6
00:02:12,369 --> 00:02:14,950
<i>If you leave your seat,
don't drink the water when you return.</i>

7
00:02:15,858 --> 00:02:17,888
<i>Tell us in the group wherever you go.</i>

8
00:02:17,888 --> 00:02:20,520
<i>Send a message every 30 minutes.</i>

9
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:22,600
<i>And if I don't?</i>

10
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:25,084
<i>I'll post a missing person notice.</i>

11
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:30,705
<i>Gosh! I'm not a child anymore.</i>

12
00:02:30,705 --> 00:02:32,928
<i>You two are being dramatic.</i>

13
00:02:32,928 --> 00:02:37,111
<i>What kind of adult meets online friends?</i>

14
00:02:37,111 --> 00:02:40,608
<i>What if you find out he's just some kid?</i>

15
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:46,496
<i>That's impossible.</i>

16
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:03,577
Where is he? There's no coser here.

17
00:03:12,235 --> 00:03:15,126
Don't tell me he really is a kid.

18
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:31,080
What are you laughing at?
Are you Commander Zhen?

19
00:03:31,080 --> 00:03:34,104
Are you YoyoLuMing?

20
00:03:34,104 --> 00:03:36,968
You have to be over 12 to play this game.

21
00:03:36,968 --> 00:03:40,471
I'm only eight. Do I look that old?

22
00:03:40,471 --> 00:03:42,005
Then why are you...

23
00:03:44,019 --> 00:03:47,964
Isn't it obvious? The Explorer.

24
00:03:47,964 --> 00:03:50,187
I'm Pao Meng, your Otherworld guide.

25
00:03:50,187 --> 00:03:52,171
Your best partner.

26
00:03:55,067 --> 00:03:56,657
Follow me.

27
00:03:58,665 --> 00:04:00,924
Adults are so boring.

28
00:04:04,084 --> 00:04:05,865
- Hi.
- Hi.

29
00:04:10,388 --> 00:04:11,532
Hi.

30
00:04:11,532 --> 00:04:13,356
- Hello.
- Hi.

31
00:04:14,931 --> 00:04:17,241
- This is for you.
- Thank you, miss.

32
00:04:22,745 --> 00:04:24,406
- Hi.
- Hi.

33
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,417
Hey, there.

34
00:04:36,691 --> 00:04:38,444
A pleasure to meet you.

35
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:50,408
I've heard of you two in Mang City.

36
00:04:57,080 --> 00:04:58,491
This way, please.

37
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:08,080
[Episode 7]
[Is Love Contagious?]

38
00:05:19,423 --> 00:05:20,839
Hello, Mr. Zeng.

39
00:05:20,839 --> 00:05:24,568
<i>The shoot is at the training center.
We've already arrived.</i>

40
00:05:25,698 --> 00:05:26,962
At the training center?

41
00:05:26,962 --> 00:05:29,640
<i>Yes. See you later.</i>

42
00:05:29,640 --> 00:05:32,000
Okay, I'll be right there.

43
00:05:47,683 --> 00:05:51,188
Ruan, the entire film team is ready.

44
00:05:51,188 --> 00:05:53,532
We won't take up
too much of your training time.

45
00:05:53,532 --> 00:05:54,970
Come on.

46
00:05:54,970 --> 00:05:56,480
We meet again, Ruan.

47
00:05:56,480 --> 00:05:59,480
I only found out yesterday
that the shoot had been changed.

48
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:00,880
But don't worry.

49
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:03,680
The new filming plan
should be within your comfort zone.

50
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:06,865
Just train as you normally would.
Pretend I'm not here.

51
00:06:06,865 --> 00:06:10,480
Our simulator trains for emergencies.
It might not be in your comfort zone.

52
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:12,880
You have your expertise, and I have mine.

53
00:06:12,880 --> 00:06:17,201
You might not know,
but we photographers thrive on challenges.

54
00:06:19,829 --> 00:06:21,613
I'm really sorry about yesterday.

55
00:06:21,613 --> 00:06:25,355
I know you don't think much of Yan An,
and you want him to give up.

56
00:06:26,004 --> 00:06:27,879
Then I should thank you.

57
00:06:31,019 --> 00:06:33,736
Let's make sure today's shoot goes smoothly.

58
00:06:34,416 --> 00:06:37,120
By the way, let me add one more thing.

59
00:06:37,120 --> 00:06:41,680
Fu Ming Yu tailored today's shoot completely
around your wishes and availability.

60
00:06:42,709 --> 00:06:44,892
How is it? Is the shoot ready?

61
00:06:44,892 --> 00:06:46,140
Ready.

62
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:52,850
Captain Fan. Thank you for your hard work.

63
00:06:52,850 --> 00:06:55,674
This shoot won't cut into anyone's break time.

64
00:06:55,674 --> 00:06:58,194
Also, maintain your usual training state.

65
00:06:58,194 --> 00:07:00,936
Okay. Let's get ready to start.

66
00:07:00,936 --> 00:07:01,940
Let's go.

67
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:04,617
- Sure.
- Let's go.

68
00:07:13,868 --> 00:07:15,652
Today's training: terrain warning.

69
00:07:15,652 --> 00:07:18,596
Hengshi Air 5101. Descend to 1,200.

70
00:07:18,596 --> 00:07:20,575
Maintain current heading.

71
00:07:22,120 --> 00:07:25,705
Maintain current heading.
Descend to 1,200. Hengshi Air 5101.

72
00:07:25,705 --> 00:07:28,226
- Descend to 1,200.
- Confirmed.

73
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:35,760
- Altitude 1,200. 39, set.
- Confirmed.

74
00:07:37,437 --> 00:07:40,100
Thrust idle, open descent. Altitude blue.

75
00:07:40,100 --> 00:07:43,006
- 12,00. 39, blue.
- Checked.

76
00:07:47,594 --> 00:07:49,417
- Maintain heading.
- Confirmed.

77
00:07:49,417 --> 00:07:51,337
- Heading.
- Checked.

78
00:08:03,587 --> 00:08:06,731
<i>Sink rate. Terrain ahead. Pull up.</i>

79
00:08:06,731 --> 00:08:08,635
- Pull up. TOGA.
<i>- Sink rate.</i>

80
00:08:08,635 --> 00:08:10,120
<i>Terrain ahead. Pull up.</i>

81
00:08:10,120 --> 00:08:12,505
Man TOGA. Autothrust blue.

82
00:08:12,505 --> 00:08:13,999
<i>Terrain ahead.</i>

83
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:18,865
Jiang City, Hengshi Air 5101. Terrain warning.

84
00:08:18,865 --> 00:08:20,121
I'm pulling up.

85
00:08:36,650 --> 00:08:37,884
Come here.

86
00:08:42,319 --> 00:08:44,170
Let me tell you two something.

87
00:08:44,170 --> 00:08:48,395
Ruan, you need to pull the thrust more slowly.

88
00:08:48,395 --> 00:08:51,495
Take it slow. Bit by bit.

89
00:09:18,440 --> 00:09:22,431
Got it? Watch your speed. Let's go.

90
00:10:19,800 --> 00:10:22,778
<i>Today's shoot went very well. Good job.</i>

91
00:10:22,778 --> 00:10:25,159
[Incoming call from Yan An]

92
00:10:29,828 --> 00:10:32,969
- Hello?
<i>- Ms. Ruan. Come over to the window.</i>

93
00:10:36,650 --> 00:10:38,092
Hang on.

94
00:10:39,818 --> 00:10:40,818
Mr. Fu.

95
00:10:41,827 --> 00:10:44,115
Are you on the phone? I'll come back in a bit.

96
00:10:44,115 --> 00:10:45,115
Okay.

97
00:10:47,615 --> 00:10:49,560
Hello? What's going on?

98
00:10:49,560 --> 00:10:51,760
<i>Are you by the window yet?</i>

99
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:54,640
The window? Which one?

100
00:10:54,640 --> 00:10:57,145
<i>The kitchen window.</i>

101
00:10:57,145 --> 00:10:58,549
The kitchen?

102
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:00,864
I'm here. Go ahead.

103
00:11:00,864 --> 00:11:04,360
<i>Tonight, I will bloom for you one last time.</i>

104
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:27,360
Si Xian! Do you see it? Is it breathtaking?

105
00:11:27,360 --> 00:11:28,580
What?

106
00:11:29,360 --> 00:11:30,720
- This is
- What did you say?

107
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:32,759
the fireworks blooming for you.

108
00:11:32,759 --> 00:11:34,759
Hello?

109
00:11:43,731 --> 00:11:45,268
This is so embarrassing.

110
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:49,865
Who is it? Did you set off the fireworks?

111
00:11:49,865 --> 00:11:51,524
No, it wasn't me! What?

112
00:11:53,498 --> 00:11:54,802
Fu Ming Yu, you jerk!

113
00:11:54,802 --> 00:11:57,227
- Stop right there!
- Don't run!

114
00:11:57,227 --> 00:11:59,160
Stop!

115
00:11:59,160 --> 00:12:01,641
- Are you crazy?
- Don't run! Cut him off.

116
00:12:10,729 --> 00:12:13,400
- Stop!
- It really wasn't me!

117
00:12:13,400 --> 00:12:14,420
- Stop!
- Don't run!

118
00:12:15,759 --> 00:12:16,759
Stop!

119
00:12:20,360 --> 00:12:21,883
You're such a jerk!

120
00:12:23,040 --> 00:12:24,606
Don't run!

121
00:12:26,480 --> 00:12:28,014
Stop!

122
00:12:30,480 --> 00:12:32,000
Grab him!

123
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:33,400
Don't touch me!

124
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:35,300
- Got him!
- Let me go!

125
00:12:44,120 --> 00:12:45,560
Officer.

126
00:12:46,920 --> 00:12:52,625
Everything I did tonight
was for everyone in our community.

127
00:12:52,625 --> 00:12:54,129
My good intentions backfired.

128
00:12:54,129 --> 00:12:56,833
I'll never do it again. Never again.

129
00:12:56,833 --> 00:12:59,561
Just leave. Don't let me see you again.

130
00:12:59,561 --> 00:13:00,601
Clean it up.

131
00:13:00,601 --> 00:13:02,583
- Don't let it become a fire hazard.
- Okay.

132
00:13:02,583 --> 00:13:04,080
Thank you.

133
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:05,670
I'm so sorry.

134
00:13:06,800 --> 00:13:09,304
I must say, you're quite photogenic.

135
00:13:09,304 --> 00:13:11,647
Fu Ming Yu, you're a real jerk.

136
00:13:11,647 --> 00:13:14,680
I'm sending your little stunt
to our group chat.

137
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:17,185
Stop trying to make a spectacle of yourself.

138
00:13:17,185 --> 00:13:19,768
This trick might have worked on your exes,

139
00:13:19,768 --> 00:13:22,845
but definitely not on Ruan Si Xian.

140
00:13:27,884 --> 00:13:29,727
I'm making a spectacle of myself?

141
00:13:30,440 --> 00:13:31,624
Fu Ming Yu, let me ask you.

142
00:13:31,624 --> 00:13:34,280
If you like Ruan Si Xian,

143
00:13:34,280 --> 00:13:36,678
why didn't you make a move on her?

144
00:13:37,520 --> 00:13:38,834
What are you afraid of?

145
00:13:40,028 --> 00:13:43,759
That she'll reject you?
Or that you can't handle losing?

146
00:13:47,625 --> 00:13:48,874
Fine.

147
00:13:49,940 --> 00:13:52,844
After tonight, I will have no chance at all.

148
00:13:52,844 --> 00:13:54,680
But I think I'm better than you.

149
00:13:55,299 --> 00:13:56,614
At least I...

150
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:01,491
had my moment.

151
00:14:31,621 --> 00:14:34,084
I just happened to mention to him that

152
00:14:34,084 --> 00:14:36,588
my friends were worried
about me meeting a stranger.

153
00:14:36,588 --> 00:14:39,093
So he called over
all the cosers he hangs out with.

154
00:14:39,093 --> 00:14:41,356
He gave me a big surprise.

155
00:14:41,356 --> 00:14:44,404
Anyway, I can tell from this that

156
00:14:44,404 --> 00:14:47,828
he's a thoughtful and attentive person.

157
00:14:47,828 --> 00:14:50,812
Anyway, it's like a dream.

158
00:14:50,812 --> 00:14:52,509
Your hands are wet.

159
00:14:54,038 --> 00:14:55,942
You think it's like a dream too?

160
00:14:55,942 --> 00:14:59,486
How can such a perfect man exist in this world?

161
00:14:59,486 --> 00:15:02,110
He checks every box. What does that mean?

162
00:15:02,110 --> 00:15:07,333
It means my balanced lifestyle
and years of good deeds finally paid off.

163
00:15:07,333 --> 00:15:09,558
I got lucky enough to get the rare one.

164
00:15:09,558 --> 00:15:10,920
Wake up.

165
00:15:10,920 --> 00:15:13,834
It just means he's humoring you.

166
00:15:16,560 --> 00:15:17,944
What?

167
00:15:17,944 --> 00:15:20,960
Ruan, you're just too rational.

168
00:15:20,960 --> 00:15:22,040
You know what?

169
00:15:22,040 --> 00:15:25,320
Athena, the goddess of wisdom,
and Venus never got along.

170
00:15:25,320 --> 00:15:28,360
So Venus's son, Cupid, the god of love,

171
00:15:28,360 --> 00:15:30,960
will never favor girls
who are too smart like you.

172
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:33,743
Where did you hear that nonsense?

173
00:15:33,743 --> 00:15:35,080
Take me as an example.

174
00:15:35,080 --> 00:15:37,960
I used to think I'd never meet
someone truly compatible with me.

175
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:42,510
But this whole thing made me realize
soulmates really do exist.

176
00:15:42,510 --> 00:15:45,215
It's just that
our lives don't always cross paths.

177
00:15:45,215 --> 00:15:49,612
So we need big data to bring them to us.

178
00:15:49,612 --> 00:15:51,557
Relying on big data for love?

179
00:15:51,557 --> 00:15:53,701
That's not reliable at all.

180
00:15:53,701 --> 00:15:57,463
People are best at
making themselves look better online.

181
00:15:57,463 --> 00:16:01,727
He could be a decent person in real life.

182
00:16:01,727 --> 00:16:04,832
And you might even share the same hobbies.

183
00:16:04,832 --> 00:16:08,175
But he may not be a good man in relationships.

184
00:16:08,175 --> 00:16:10,160
- No--
- Remember.

185
00:16:10,160 --> 00:16:14,336
Good men don't show up in big data.

186
00:16:14,336 --> 00:16:15,599
I disagree.

187
00:16:15,599 --> 00:16:18,223
A good man could be waiting for the right girl.

188
00:16:18,223 --> 00:16:19,847
- Why are you everywhere?
- You're--

189
00:16:19,847 --> 00:16:21,880
Get lost.

190
00:16:21,880 --> 00:16:24,463
Ignore him. Just remember what I said.

191
00:16:24,463 --> 00:16:27,360
Don't let him cheat you out of everything.

192
00:16:27,360 --> 00:16:28,825
What's there to cheat me out of?

193
00:16:28,825 --> 00:16:30,888
Forget it. I won't explain it to you two.

194
00:16:30,888 --> 00:16:33,830
I'll bring them here another day
so you can meet them.

195
00:16:34,418 --> 00:16:36,160
- Them?
- Them?

196
00:16:36,160 --> 00:16:39,000
Him. A slip of the tongue.

197
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:40,440
You got my hopes up for nothing.

198
00:16:40,440 --> 00:16:41,745
Rag!

199
00:16:51,944 --> 00:16:53,228
Oh my god.

200
00:16:55,563 --> 00:16:58,178
What do you think? Do you like this one?

201
00:16:58,178 --> 00:17:02,857
If not, we can see more this afternoon.
I really can't walk anymore.

202
00:17:05,460 --> 00:17:08,243
Just give me a straight answer.

203
00:17:08,243 --> 00:17:10,186
If you don't like it, let's just go eat.

204
00:17:10,186 --> 00:17:12,277
We'll see the rest tomorrow.

205
00:17:13,600 --> 00:17:15,513
Can you keep it down?

206
00:17:15,513 --> 00:17:18,040
If the agent hears you, how can I bargain?

207
00:17:18,040 --> 00:17:20,270
You're thinking about bargaining?

208
00:17:20,270 --> 00:17:22,615
Buddy, we'll take this one.

209
00:17:22,615 --> 00:17:24,680
Who said we're taking it?

210
00:17:24,680 --> 00:17:27,385
I have a few more questions.

211
00:17:27,385 --> 00:17:29,800
Don't listen to her. She'll try to haggle.

212
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:32,745
Miss, we really can't lower the price here.

213
00:17:32,745 --> 00:17:34,957
It's settled then.

214
00:17:36,040 --> 00:17:39,223
The two of us have shown you places all day.

215
00:17:39,223 --> 00:17:42,440
We've seen all kinds of houses.
Don't make it hard for him.

216
00:17:42,440 --> 00:17:45,425
Just let me spend more
so I can feel better. Okay?

217
00:17:45,425 --> 00:17:48,319
I'm recovering from a breakup.
I just want to spend money.

218
00:17:48,319 --> 00:17:50,440
- Please.
- Stop it.

219
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:54,868
I'm not making it hard for you,
so don't do the same to me.

220
00:17:55,601 --> 00:17:57,855
My family's situation...

221
00:18:00,945 --> 00:18:02,840
It's none of your business anyway.

222
00:18:05,079 --> 00:18:06,640
It's fine.

223
00:18:06,640 --> 00:18:09,759
I know that funds are tight
in the early startup stage.

224
00:18:09,759 --> 00:18:13,759
But for this house's rent,
consider it my initial investment.

225
00:18:13,759 --> 00:18:16,526
I have great faith in you.

226
00:18:23,320 --> 00:18:26,586
Ms. Zheng, most importantly,

227
00:18:27,844 --> 00:18:33,465
I think this house matches your aura perfectly.

228
00:18:34,307 --> 00:18:35,834
How so?

229
00:18:38,347 --> 00:18:40,252
First, look at this space.

230
00:18:40,252 --> 00:18:42,955
It's perfect for you as a photo studio.

231
00:18:42,955 --> 00:18:46,284
Secondly, look at the windows on this side.

232
00:18:49,960 --> 00:18:52,124
What's planted outside?

233
00:18:52,124 --> 00:18:55,360
Bamboo. Chinese style.
What does that represent?

234
00:18:55,360 --> 00:18:59,505
Your background, your nationality.

235
00:18:59,505 --> 00:19:02,375
It represents where you come from.

236
00:19:03,120 --> 00:19:05,624
Now, turn around and look back.

237
00:19:05,624 --> 00:19:07,769
That silver crystal chandelier.

238
00:19:07,769 --> 00:19:10,200
It's European style. What does that represent?

239
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:12,784
Your experience studying photography.

240
00:19:12,784 --> 00:19:18,746
It subtly reflects your roots and your past.

241
00:19:18,746 --> 00:19:20,810
It's practically made for you.

242
00:19:20,810 --> 00:19:24,153
In all of Jiang City, this is one of a kind.

243
00:19:24,153 --> 00:19:27,851
Isn't this house great?
It's such a bargain. Let's take it.

244
00:19:28,516 --> 00:19:29,516
No.

245
00:19:30,256 --> 00:19:33,480
I already lost 30,000 yuan.

246
00:19:33,480 --> 00:19:38,383
It's on me.
I, Yan An, should pay for my impulsiveness.

247
00:19:38,383 --> 00:19:39,888
Sign it.

248
00:19:39,888 --> 00:19:41,561
- But I still think--
- Here.

249
00:20:08,075 --> 00:20:10,740
I thought we'd meet at an internet cafe.

250
00:20:10,740 --> 00:20:15,120
He can't seriously expect us
to be his cheerleaders, right?

251
00:20:17,452 --> 00:20:20,115
So which of us is playing good cop later?

252
00:20:20,115 --> 00:20:21,979
I think we should both be bad cops.

253
00:20:21,979 --> 00:20:23,963
We must let him know that
although Xiao Zhen is naive,

254
00:20:23,963 --> 00:20:26,116
her friends aren't just for show.

255
00:20:27,130 --> 00:20:28,451
He's here.

256
00:20:29,921 --> 00:20:31,544
You're here.

257
00:20:34,941 --> 00:20:39,240
Let me introduce you.
This is my gamer carry, Lu Ming.

258
00:20:39,240 --> 00:20:40,640
Nice to meet you.

259
00:20:42,267 --> 00:20:45,499
They're Ruan and Xuan, my best friends.

260
00:20:46,240 --> 00:20:48,701
Oh, right. I brought drinks for you.

261
00:20:49,467 --> 00:20:51,103
Please, help yourselves.

262
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:53,300
That's very thoughtful.

263
00:20:56,280 --> 00:20:57,760
Shall we go play then?

264
00:20:57,760 --> 00:20:59,040
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

265
00:21:04,740 --> 00:21:06,116
Are you ready?

266
00:21:06,840 --> 00:21:10,744
Pass it to me.

267
00:21:10,744 --> 00:21:11,954
Catch!

268
00:21:13,587 --> 00:21:14,851
Xiao Zhen.

269
00:21:16,810 --> 00:21:18,539
One, two, three.

270
00:21:20,322 --> 00:21:21,720
I can't do it.

271
00:21:21,720 --> 00:21:23,185
Use less force. Let's try again.

272
00:21:23,185 --> 00:21:25,466
- Okay.
- Come on.

273
00:21:25,466 --> 00:21:27,210
- Are you ready?
- Ready.

274
00:21:27,210 --> 00:21:29,720
Why are we standing here?

275
00:21:29,720 --> 00:21:31,243
I have no idea.

276
00:21:37,579 --> 00:21:39,002
- Nice shot!
- I'm so good!

277
00:21:39,002 --> 00:21:40,946
Just throw it like that. Got it?

278
00:21:40,946 --> 00:21:42,651
Let's try one more time.

279
00:21:42,651 --> 00:21:45,311
- You're really good.
- You're a great teacher.

280
00:21:49,010 --> 00:21:52,104
Why are we sitting here now?

281
00:21:52,104 --> 00:21:52,897
Like this?

282
00:21:52,897 --> 00:21:54,600
Better than standing.

283
00:21:54,600 --> 00:21:56,720
- Like this?
- Yes.

284
00:21:56,720 --> 00:21:59,519
Now, try it. One, two, three.

285
00:21:59,519 --> 00:22:02,039
No, not like that.

286
00:22:02,039 --> 00:22:05,240
How many good deeds did our Xiao Zhen do?

287
00:22:05,240 --> 00:22:07,079
She really hit the jackpot.

288
00:22:07,079 --> 00:22:08,440
But how do I lift it?

289
00:22:08,440 --> 00:22:10,640
I don't blame Xiao Zhen.

290
00:22:10,640 --> 00:22:12,680
Anyone would fall head over heels for him.

291
00:22:12,680 --> 00:22:14,359
Hold it a bit higher.

292
00:22:14,359 --> 00:22:15,720
Is this basketball?

293
00:22:15,720 --> 00:22:17,920
Look at their eyes.

294
00:22:17,920 --> 00:22:20,358
I must say, it's pretty sweet.

295
00:22:22,279 --> 00:22:23,462
Come on, aim.

296
00:22:23,462 --> 00:22:26,799
What do you think?
Don't you think being in love seems nice?

297
00:22:26,799 --> 00:22:28,079
Give it a try.

298
00:22:28,079 --> 00:22:32,000
I'm not a three-year-old.
I don't want everything I see.

299
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:36,000
All my energy goes into flying planes.

300
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:38,631
Dating has nothing to do with me.

301
00:22:39,334 --> 00:22:43,680
You didn't date before because you said
you had to focus on becoming a pilot.

302
00:22:43,680 --> 00:22:46,664
Now that you're a pilot,
you say you need to focus on flying.

303
00:22:46,664 --> 00:22:49,569
Are you planning to wait until retirement?

304
00:22:49,569 --> 00:22:54,472
I just feel that in modern society,
no one is indispensable.

305
00:22:54,472 --> 00:22:56,497
Even without dating, life is still pretty good.

306
00:22:56,497 --> 00:22:59,281
I think that mindset is quite dangerous.

307
00:22:59,281 --> 00:23:01,785
We should be prepared to walk away at any time,

308
00:23:01,785 --> 00:23:05,520
but don't shut out someone
who gives you their heart.

309
00:23:05,520 --> 00:23:09,400
Who gives their heart? Yan An?

310
00:23:09,400 --> 00:23:11,184
Give me a break.

311
00:23:11,184 --> 00:23:14,334
I'm not talking about him.

312
00:23:19,411 --> 00:23:21,411
<i>Why did you come to Hengshi Air?</i>

313
00:23:24,732 --> 00:23:26,163
<i>For me?</i>

314
00:23:28,099 --> 00:23:29,710
What's wrong?

315
00:23:30,560 --> 00:23:33,040
- What's going on?
- Nothing.

316
00:23:33,040 --> 00:23:35,859
I think I've been dazed by the fireworks.

317
00:23:37,867 --> 00:23:41,012
Hey, beauties. It's boring just sitting here.

318
00:23:41,012 --> 00:23:42,235
Come and play with us.

319
00:23:42,235 --> 00:23:43,708
- No, thanks.
- No, thanks.

320
00:23:44,587 --> 00:23:47,451
It's my first time seeing
a 'lift-style' shot. Very creative.

321
00:23:47,451 --> 00:23:49,076
Are you being sarcastic?

322
00:23:49,076 --> 00:23:51,280
It's fine. I don't mind.

323
00:23:51,280 --> 00:23:54,520
At least it proves
he's not what you two thought.

324
00:23:54,520 --> 00:23:59,623
Should we give you two some privacy?

325
00:23:59,623 --> 00:24:03,447
Does it even matter if we step away now?

326
00:24:03,447 --> 00:24:04,912
You two really...

327
00:24:04,912 --> 00:24:07,975
It's only the second time I've met him.

328
00:24:07,975 --> 00:24:11,560
Only the second time?
What were you doing just now?

329
00:24:11,560 --> 00:24:13,400
- A lift-shot.
- A lift-shot!

330
00:24:13,400 --> 00:24:16,800
Well... We're just friends for now.

331
00:24:16,800 --> 00:24:18,960
I wonder what he's actually thinking.

332
00:24:18,960 --> 00:24:22,584
Don't worry. At least it's not unrequited love.

333
00:24:22,584 --> 00:24:24,864
Really?

334
00:24:25,817 --> 00:24:28,120
Then I'm going to confess.

335
00:24:28,120 --> 00:24:31,305
Confess what? You need to stay calm.

336
00:24:31,305 --> 00:24:33,840
If he's into you, he'll make the first move.

337
00:24:33,840 --> 00:24:37,784
But... Ruan just said it's not one-sided.

338
00:24:37,784 --> 00:24:39,808
He must be interested in me.

339
00:24:39,808 --> 00:24:42,392
Even if he is, he's keeping his cool.

340
00:24:42,392 --> 00:24:45,567
My advice is to wait a bit longer.

341
00:24:45,567 --> 00:24:48,081
Good things come to those who wait.

342
00:24:48,720 --> 00:24:50,261
Alright then.

343
00:24:51,706 --> 00:24:53,331
I'll head back over there.

344
00:24:53,331 --> 00:24:55,960
Lu Ming said he'd treat us
to a late-night snack.

345
00:24:55,960 --> 00:24:58,103
Good things come to those who wait.

346
00:24:58,103 --> 00:24:59,966
I'll pass.

347
00:24:59,966 --> 00:25:02,227
I have to get up early.
I have a flight tomorrow.

348
00:25:03,680 --> 00:25:05,470
There'll be plenty of chances.

349
00:25:06,218 --> 00:25:10,200
Xuan, I'm leaving the "child" to you.

350
00:25:10,200 --> 00:25:11,600
Bye-bye.

351
00:25:15,445 --> 00:25:17,269
Then I'll... be off.

352
00:25:17,269 --> 00:25:18,688
Go ahead.

353
00:25:21,240 --> 00:25:24,130
- You're back.
- Come. You must be thirsty.

354
00:25:24,130 --> 00:25:25,559
Here.

355
00:25:25,559 --> 00:25:28,565
Leave the kid to me,
and you can start worrying.

356
00:25:36,651 --> 00:25:38,574
<i>You're back so late.</i>

357
00:25:42,547 --> 00:25:44,306
<i>Have you been drinking?</i>

358
00:25:56,120 --> 00:25:57,960
You didn't fly today?

359
00:26:07,060 --> 00:26:08,548
Aren't you getting off?

360
00:26:09,346 --> 00:26:12,287
Oh no. I'm losing my mind.

361
00:26:13,240 --> 00:26:16,074
Why is he everywhere I go?

362
00:26:35,641 --> 00:26:37,062
It's warm.

363
00:26:38,668 --> 00:26:40,349
Are you...

364
00:26:41,276 --> 00:26:42,980
Fu Ming Yu?

365
00:26:42,980 --> 00:26:46,028
Who else? Do you think I'm Jay Chou?

366
00:26:46,028 --> 00:26:50,372
If you have mental issues,
I suggest you get help.

367
00:26:50,372 --> 00:26:51,715
Why are you here?

368
00:26:51,715 --> 00:26:54,160
I'm going home after work. Shouldn't I be here?

369
00:26:54,160 --> 00:26:57,400
You, on the other hand,
came to B1 without getting off.

370
00:26:58,259 --> 00:26:59,868
Why are you here?

371
00:27:04,850 --> 00:27:05,850
<i>Mr. Fu.</i>

372
00:27:07,131 --> 00:27:09,692
<i>Are you on the phone? I'll come back later.</i>

373
00:27:12,751 --> 00:27:18,611
I just remembered. When you came to
my place that night, did you need something?

374
00:27:27,040 --> 00:27:30,266
Yan An. It's Yan An.
He said he'd set off fireworks that day.

375
00:27:30,266 --> 00:27:33,474
I wanted to give you a heads-up.
So he couldn't fool you.

376
00:27:33,474 --> 00:27:35,360
That's his usual trick for pursuing girls.

377
00:27:35,360 --> 00:27:37,440
Then what's your trick?

378
00:27:41,362 --> 00:27:42,466
What?

379
00:27:45,218 --> 00:27:46,747
Want to find out?

380
00:27:50,156 --> 00:27:52,701
I'm home. I'll get going.

381
00:27:52,701 --> 00:27:53,865
Wait.

382
00:27:55,244 --> 00:27:56,244
Yes?

383
00:27:56,875 --> 00:28:00,086
This is the 29th floor. I should get off first.

384
00:28:13,680 --> 00:28:17,320
[Jiang City]

385
00:28:31,108 --> 00:28:33,783
How do you feel about your first solo flight?

386
00:28:34,828 --> 00:28:38,955
I'm excited. But also a bit nervous.

387
00:28:38,955 --> 00:28:41,428
It's okay. Call me if you need help.

388
00:28:46,651 --> 00:28:48,451
Mommy.

389
00:28:49,209 --> 00:28:51,509
<i>It's our busiest time. You're taking leave now?</i>

390
00:28:52,332 --> 00:28:54,757
I am, but I'm not neglecting my work.

391
00:28:54,757 --> 00:28:58,080
Besides, I've been staying up
several nights on this proposal.

392
00:28:58,080 --> 00:29:00,240
I took annual leave to take my child home.

393
00:29:00,240 --> 00:29:06,025
<i>Flight HS2076 from Jiang City to Shen City
is now ready for boarding.</i>

394
00:29:06,025 --> 00:29:07,369
<i>Please have your boarding passes ready.</i>

395
00:29:07,369 --> 00:29:11,240
Boarding now. Landing in two and a half hours.
I'll text you then, okay?

396
00:29:11,240 --> 00:29:12,440
Okay.

397
00:29:17,915 --> 00:29:20,100
Come here. Let Mommy hold you.

398
00:29:20,100 --> 00:29:22,176
Let's go. We're ready to board.

399
00:29:38,640 --> 00:29:40,880
It's okay. Don't cry.

400
00:29:40,880 --> 00:29:43,120
- Mommy.
- I'm here. Just a second.

401
00:29:43,120 --> 00:29:45,960
- Mommy.
- Welcome aboard, ma'am.

402
00:29:45,960 --> 00:29:48,687
- There, there. Don't cry.
- Ma'am.

403
00:29:48,687 --> 00:29:49,893
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

404
00:29:49,893 --> 00:29:51,559
- Hello.
- It's further back.

405
00:29:52,146 --> 00:29:53,280
Hello.

406
00:29:53,280 --> 00:29:54,400
Thank you.

407
00:29:55,200 --> 00:29:57,360
- Let me help you with that. Careful.
- Careful.

408
00:29:57,360 --> 00:29:58,600
- Okay.
- Welcome aboard, little one.

409
00:29:58,600 --> 00:30:01,648
- Hello. Where is your seat?
- This one right here.

410
00:30:01,648 --> 00:30:03,428
Let me help you.

411
00:30:04,680 --> 00:30:06,151
Welcome aboard.

412
00:30:07,122 --> 00:30:08,822
Hello, welcome aboard.

413
00:30:13,840 --> 00:30:15,120
Thank you.

414
00:30:16,203 --> 00:30:18,691
This is the infant seat belt.
Please fasten it before takeoff.

415
00:30:18,691 --> 00:30:19,691
Okay.

416
00:30:26,200 --> 00:30:28,680
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,</i>

417
00:30:28,680 --> 00:30:30,519
<i>thank you for your patience.</i>

418
00:30:30,519 --> 00:30:33,119
<i>This flight is about to taxi for takeoff.</i>

419
00:30:33,119 --> 00:30:34,559
<i>To ensure your safety...</i>

420
00:30:34,559 --> 00:30:36,559
- Mommy.
<i>- Please stow your tray tables,</i>

421
00:30:36,559 --> 00:30:38,839
<i>return your seat to the upright position,
and open your window shade.</i>

422
00:30:38,839 --> 00:30:41,640
What a troublesome kid.
She just won't settle down.

423
00:30:41,640 --> 00:30:45,319
I don't get it.
Why bring kids along when traveling?

424
00:30:45,319 --> 00:30:47,599
There, there. Duo Duo, be good. Stop crying.

425
00:30:47,599 --> 00:30:49,500
<i>Or switch them to airplane mode.</i>

426
00:30:50,352 --> 00:30:51,360
Excuse me, ma'am.

427
00:30:51,360 --> 00:30:53,559
During takeoff and landing,
the baby might feel ear pressure.

428
00:30:53,559 --> 00:30:56,480
I suggest you give her some water.
It'll help ease the discomfort.

429
00:30:56,480 --> 00:31:00,079
Okay. Here, drink some water. Good girl.

430
00:31:00,079 --> 00:31:02,353
Drink some water, good girl.

431
00:31:02,353 --> 00:31:03,720
- Swallow it.
- Thank you.

432
00:31:03,720 --> 00:31:06,944
- Ma'am. For large equipment like this--
- I just need a minute.

433
00:31:06,944 --> 00:31:08,529
Wait, just one minute.

434
00:31:08,529 --> 00:31:10,320
Ma'am, we're about to take off.

435
00:31:10,320 --> 00:31:12,881
Using this now is unsafe.
Here, let me help you.

436
00:31:12,881 --> 00:31:14,920
No, I'm good. You handle that one.

437
00:31:14,920 --> 00:31:16,398
Alright.

438
00:31:16,398 --> 00:31:18,759
Sorry, ma'am, but we need to hurry.

439
00:31:18,759 --> 00:31:19,799
Okay.

440
00:31:19,799 --> 00:31:22,440
Let me help you. Fasten your seat belt.

441
00:31:22,440 --> 00:31:23,840
- Thank you.
- Give her more water.

442
00:31:23,840 --> 00:31:26,519
If you need anything, press the button above.

443
00:31:26,519 --> 00:31:27,839
Okay. Thank you.

444
00:32:01,520 --> 00:32:03,640
Excuse me, my computer.

445
00:32:03,640 --> 00:32:06,039
Your kid is so noisy.
Can you do something about it?

446
00:32:06,039 --> 00:32:07,273
I'm sorry.

447
00:32:08,080 --> 00:32:10,104
So annoying. Can't you just let me sleep?

448
00:32:10,104 --> 00:32:11,608
I'm just trying to catch up on sleep.

449
00:32:11,608 --> 00:32:13,431
- Exactly.
- Oh my goodness.

450
00:32:13,431 --> 00:32:15,616
This kid's voice is raising my blood pressure.

451
00:32:15,616 --> 00:32:17,840
- I know, right? My god.
- I'm sorry.

452
00:32:17,840 --> 00:32:21,519
Sorry. Her ears hurt from the flight.
She'll be fine once she falls asleep.

453
00:32:21,519 --> 00:32:23,799
Go to sleep, Duo Duo. Be good.

454
00:32:23,799 --> 00:32:26,500
- You'll understand when you have children.
- Duo Duo, be good and go to sleep.

455
00:32:29,947 --> 00:32:33,572
Mentor, that kid in the back is really loud.

456
00:32:33,572 --> 00:32:34,915
Like Ne Zha reincarnated.

457
00:32:34,915 --> 00:32:37,659
When she stirs up the sea,
the passengers in the front get dizzy too.

458
00:32:37,659 --> 00:32:40,512
- What about the back?
- It's even worse back there.

459
00:32:40,512 --> 00:32:41,840
The call bells keep ringing.

460
00:32:41,840 --> 00:32:44,520
- Ding, ding, nonstop.
- Could it be worse than the summer rush?

461
00:32:44,520 --> 00:32:47,776
Mentor, it's practically the summer rush.

462
00:32:49,356 --> 00:32:54,164
Ruan, once you pass your line check next week,
you'll be able to fly the line.

463
00:32:54,164 --> 00:32:58,428
I'll speak with crew scheduling in advance
so I can take you on your first flight.

464
00:32:58,428 --> 00:33:00,171
Thank you, mentor.

465
00:33:00,171 --> 00:33:02,475
After today's flight, let's take a photo.

466
00:33:02,475 --> 00:33:05,200
You're the only two female pilots
in our company.

467
00:33:05,200 --> 00:33:07,440
Who knows when we'll fly together again.

468
00:33:07,440 --> 00:33:08,600
No problem.

469
00:33:08,600 --> 00:33:12,223
- Mentor, Yu, I'm going to the restroom.
- Go ahead.

470
00:33:16,640 --> 00:33:18,640
Cover for Ruan Si Xian.
She's using the restroom.

471
00:33:18,640 --> 00:33:20,080
Okay, got it.

472
00:33:20,080 --> 00:33:22,060
You go ahead. I'll check on you later.

473
00:33:39,452 --> 00:33:40,841
Be good.

474
00:33:43,520 --> 00:33:46,164
Duo Duo, sit here by yourself for a while.

475
00:33:46,164 --> 00:33:48,334
Mommy's going to the restroom.

476
00:34:02,874 --> 00:34:05,059
Ma'am, can I help you?

477
00:34:05,059 --> 00:34:06,922
I don't feel well. I need to use the restroom.

478
00:34:06,922 --> 00:34:09,146
Ma'am, the restroom is currently occupied.

479
00:34:09,146 --> 00:34:11,800
Please wait a moment.
What seems to be the problem?

480
00:34:11,800 --> 00:34:13,624
I feel a bit nauseous.

481
00:34:13,624 --> 00:34:14,624
Ma'am.

482
00:34:15,800 --> 00:34:17,488
Ma'am. Ma'am!

483
00:34:17,488 --> 00:34:19,427
- What's happening?
- Are you okay?

484
00:34:22,280 --> 00:34:23,840
Ma'am.

485
00:34:23,840 --> 00:34:26,623
- What's the situation?
- Mentor, this lady fainted.

486
00:34:26,623 --> 00:34:29,560
Move her to the front cabin.
Prepare for first aid.

487
00:34:29,560 --> 00:34:30,945
- Sorry for the trouble.
- It's okay.

488
00:34:30,945 --> 00:34:32,325
Excuse me.

489
00:34:33,440 --> 00:34:35,000
What's the situation in the back?

490
00:34:35,000 --> 00:34:36,280
A passenger suddenly fainted.

491
00:34:36,280 --> 00:34:38,800
She's clutching her chest.
It looks like a heart problem.

492
00:34:41,379 --> 00:34:45,244
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,
we have an unwell passenger.</i>

493
00:34:45,244 --> 00:34:49,547
<i>If you are a medical professional,
please contact the cabin crew immediately.</i>

494
00:34:49,547 --> 00:34:50,643
<i>Thank you.</i>

495
00:34:52,120 --> 00:34:54,344
Excuse me, ma'am. Please let this lady through.

496
00:34:54,344 --> 00:34:57,480
Thank you.

497
00:35:01,719 --> 00:35:03,676
There, there.

498
00:35:05,240 --> 00:35:06,840
- Are you a doctor?
- Yes.

499
00:35:06,840 --> 00:35:07,840
Please.

500
00:35:19,961 --> 00:35:21,704
Are you looking for your mommy?

501
00:35:22,519 --> 00:35:24,480
There, there, don't cry.

502
00:35:24,480 --> 00:35:26,519
Excuse me, what's happening up there?

503
00:35:26,519 --> 00:35:28,556
It's alright, ma'am. Please don't panic.

504
00:35:35,916 --> 00:35:38,362
Signs point to a heart attack.
She needs medical attention immediately.

505
00:35:38,362 --> 00:35:41,406
I'm performing CPR on her now.
I need your assistance.

506
00:35:47,400 --> 00:35:50,625
Captain Fan, the doctor on board says
it's a heart attack.

507
00:35:50,625 --> 00:35:52,209
<i>The patient needs immediate treatment.</i>

508
00:35:52,209 --> 00:35:53,349
Got it.

509
00:35:55,035 --> 00:35:57,939
Given the situation,
we can't continue to our destination.

510
00:35:57,939 --> 00:36:01,280
We'll return to Jiang City for landing.
Weather meets landing standards.

511
00:36:01,280 --> 00:36:03,505
Fuel is sufficient.
We can consider an overweight landing.

512
00:36:03,505 --> 00:36:05,560
It's our main operations base.
We'll have full ground support.

513
00:36:05,560 --> 00:36:07,722
- Ruan, calculate the landing performance.
- Copy that.

514
00:36:07,722 --> 00:36:09,520
Jiang City, Hengshi Air 2076.

515
00:36:09,520 --> 00:36:11,080
<i>Hengshi Air 2076, go ahead.</i>

516
00:36:11,080 --> 00:36:14,640
A passenger has fainted on board.
A doctor is currently treating her.

517
00:36:14,640 --> 00:36:18,073
But immediate emergency care is needed.
Request return to Jiang City and radar vectors.

518
00:36:18,073 --> 00:36:20,218
Please notify our company
and relevant departments.

519
00:36:20,218 --> 00:36:21,800
<i>Hengshi Air 2076, roger.</i>

520
00:36:21,800 --> 00:36:24,646
<i>Radar vectors. Turn right heading 210.
Descend to 4,200.</i>

521
00:36:24,646 --> 00:36:27,870
Right turn heading 210.
Descend to 4,200. Hengshi Air 2076.

522
00:36:27,870 --> 00:36:29,870
- Descend to 4,200.
- Confirmed.

523
00:36:31,376 --> 00:36:33,520
- 4,200. 138, set.
- Confirmed.

524
00:36:33,520 --> 00:36:35,720
Thrust idle, open descent. Altitude blue.

525
00:36:35,720 --> 00:36:38,704
- 4,200. 138, blue.
- Checked.

526
00:36:38,704 --> 00:36:40,087
Turn right heading 210.

527
00:36:40,087 --> 00:36:41,312
Confirmed.

528
00:36:41,312 --> 00:36:43,752
- Heading 210 blue.
- Checked.

529
00:36:47,628 --> 00:36:51,051
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,
this is your purser speaking.</i>

530
00:36:51,051 --> 00:36:55,546
<i>Due to a medical emergency on board,
the captain has decided to return immediately.</i>

531
00:36:55,546 --> 00:36:58,427
We sincerely apologize for the inconvenience.

532
00:36:58,427 --> 00:37:00,320
<i>Thank you for your understanding.</i>

533
00:37:00,320 --> 00:37:02,160
I'm in a hurry.

534
00:37:02,160 --> 00:37:04,260
Your mommy will be here soon.

535
00:37:05,226 --> 00:37:06,525
Mommy.

536
00:37:40,600 --> 00:37:42,703
How long until we land? The patient can't wait.

537
00:37:42,703 --> 00:37:43,904
I'll go ask.

538
00:37:47,723 --> 00:37:50,906
Captain, the patient is in critical condition
and needs an immediate landing.

539
00:37:50,906 --> 00:37:52,651
<i>How much longer will it take?</i>

540
00:37:52,651 --> 00:37:54,739
It'll take over 20 minutes.

541
00:37:56,946 --> 00:37:59,891
<i>Hengshi Air 2076, contact Approach on 125.55.</i>

542
00:37:59,891 --> 00:38:02,470
125.55, Hengshi Air 2076.

543
00:38:04,538 --> 00:38:07,082
The more urgent it is, the calmer we must be.

544
00:38:07,082 --> 00:38:09,506
While we race against time for the patient,

545
00:38:09,506 --> 00:38:14,682
we are also responsible for the safety
of the other 181 passengers on board.

546
00:38:14,682 --> 00:38:16,722
- Prepare for approach.
- Roger.

547
00:38:21,732 --> 00:38:23,116
Have you contacted the patient's family?

548
00:38:23,116 --> 00:38:25,699
<i>Yes, we have. But none of them are local.</i>

549
00:38:25,699 --> 00:38:27,159
What's the current situation?

550
00:38:27,159 --> 00:38:30,920
<i>The crew is doing their best to return.
A doctor on board is performing CPR.</i>

551
00:38:30,920 --> 00:38:34,760
<i>They don't have time to burn fuel.
They'll likely land overweight.</i>

552
00:38:34,760 --> 00:38:36,760
<i>The ambulance is on standby near the runway.</i>

553
00:38:36,760 --> 00:38:38,000
Who's the captain?

554
00:38:38,000 --> 00:38:39,699
Fan Lei, Yu Yang Ming...

555
00:38:41,000 --> 00:38:42,357
and Ruan Si Xian.

556
00:38:45,261 --> 00:38:47,044
I'm on my way there.

557
00:38:47,044 --> 00:38:51,508
Listen. Hengshi Air's safety record must stand.

558
00:38:51,508 --> 00:38:52,703
Understood.

559
00:38:54,443 --> 00:38:57,931
Captain, the patient's condition is worsening.
She needs immediate care.

560
00:38:57,931 --> 00:39:00,312
<i>Any further delay could be life-threatening.</i>

561
00:39:22,800 --> 00:39:24,240
Okay, I got it.

562
00:39:24,240 --> 00:39:27,200
- No more calls. We land in ten minutes.
- Roger.

563
00:39:29,668 --> 00:39:32,051
Disconnect the autopilot. I have control.

564
00:39:32,051 --> 00:39:33,515
The timing should be about right.

565
00:39:33,515 --> 00:39:35,440
Should we disconnect it? No need, right?

566
00:39:35,440 --> 00:39:38,505
With autopilot engaged,
the bank angle is limited to 30 degrees.

567
00:39:38,505 --> 00:39:40,009
I'm disconnecting for manual flight.

568
00:39:40,009 --> 00:39:41,560
- I'll keep bank angle below 45 degrees.
- No.

569
00:39:41,560 --> 00:39:43,480
Exceeding 30 degrees will trigger the QAR.

570
00:39:43,480 --> 00:39:47,079
Three turns will save at least 15 minutes.
There's no time. Listen to me.

571
00:39:47,079 --> 00:39:49,880
- Mentor.
- Contact the tower to prepare for landing.

572
00:39:49,880 --> 00:39:51,440
I'll take full responsibility.

573
00:39:51,440 --> 00:39:54,483
Approach checklist.
Overweight landing checklist.

574
00:39:59,464 --> 00:40:02,500
Category III. Category I.

575
00:40:02,500 --> 00:40:03,500
Checked.

576
00:40:38,627 --> 00:40:39,930
Request a right turn.

577
00:40:39,930 --> 00:40:42,835
Tower, Hengshi Air 2076 requests a right turn.

578
00:40:42,835 --> 00:40:44,578
<i>Hengshi Air 2076, cleared for right turn.</i>

579
00:40:44,578 --> 00:40:46,320
<i>ILS Runway 04. Report established.</i>

580
00:40:46,320 --> 00:40:48,039
<i>Cleared for right turn. ILS Runway 04.</i>

581
00:40:48,039 --> 00:40:49,760
<i>Report established. Hengshi Air 2076.</i>

582
00:40:49,760 --> 00:40:51,340
Prepare for approach.

583
00:41:11,040 --> 00:41:13,540
Why is the plane turning?

584
00:41:14,171 --> 00:41:17,000
- Flaps full.
- Speed checked. Flaps full.

585
00:41:17,000 --> 00:41:18,280
Landing checklist.

586
00:41:26,160 --> 00:41:28,639
- Landing.
- Checked.

587
00:41:28,639 --> 00:41:30,560
- One hundred above.
- Checked.

588
00:41:30,560 --> 00:41:32,420
- Minimums.
- Continue.

589
00:41:39,960 --> 00:41:44,281
Fifty. Forty. Thirty. Twenty.

590
00:41:46,267 --> 00:41:47,560
Spoilers.

591
00:41:49,880 --> 00:41:51,576
Decelerating.

592
00:43:13,840 --> 00:43:17,064
Don't worry.
The passenger has been resuscitated.

593
00:43:17,064 --> 00:43:18,968
And her family has arrived at the hospital.

594
00:43:18,968 --> 00:43:21,440
They want to give our crew
an appreciation banner.

595
00:43:21,440 --> 00:43:22,440
I see.

596
00:43:23,040 --> 00:43:25,344
Then what about the Safety Committee?

597
00:43:25,344 --> 00:43:28,364
Let's wait.
We'll see the captain's report first.

598
00:43:29,017 --> 00:43:31,597
Okay. Let me brief you.

599
00:43:32,339 --> 00:43:34,923
The flight has resumed its normal operations.

600
00:43:34,923 --> 00:43:38,186
But it'll be two hours late to the destination.

601
00:43:40,577 --> 00:43:44,041
Treat the whole crew
to dinner tonight in my name.

602
00:43:44,041 --> 00:43:45,832
Okay, I'll arrange it.

